dots, with the caveat that those dots can only be used to create Wonders until the remaining cost is paid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I had no idea, what page is this on, any idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T23:42:28-08:00","id":1160137,"title":"","content":"I had no idea that the ecstatic constantly have sensory effects on, that strikes me as not only broken but also overwhelming for the characters in question. <br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 11-18-2017, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T23:50:23-08:00","id":1160139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1158813-tradition-specific-abilities?p=1158886#post1158886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I fucking love your signature!<br /> <br /> Hilarious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T00:34:23-08:00","id":1160145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1158813-tradition-specific-abilities?p=1160136#post1160136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I had no idea, what page is this on, any idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sons of Ether Revised Tradition Book, p. 65.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T18:39:01-08:00","id":1160383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1158813-tradition-specific-abilities?p=1160137#post1160137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had no idea that the ecstatic constantly have sensory effects on, that strikes me as not only broken but also overwhelming for the characters in question.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>One effect is free per CoX first edition tradition book, page 65. Of course, since they are on, the sensory effects of loud senses are doubled. So, if someone has Forces on, they are going to notice that bright light flash or booming sound more and might have to use Willpower to not be overwhelmed. <br /> <br /> As for being broken, Cultists are kinda of weird at seeing things and other perceptions may be altered by focusing on using sphere perceptions. I doubt it breaks the game to limit perceptions. If it does, then consider whether the game is right by being broken.<br /> <br /> I say the view on perceptions can be an issue for some games because I've seen games where divination and sense magic can quickly solve puzzles and allow targeting and provides an edge to players who know how to use it. However, I've seen D&amp;D style games were all the rooms had lead alloys in the wall to stop divination and it required a suspension of disbelief beyond me. Basically, the scenario was intended to hose any attempts at divination. That sounds like denying players a tool completely, which may not be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T09:10:51-08:00","id":1160881,"title":"","content":"Are you including implicit benefits of certain groups like the less-paradox-prone aspects of technomagic? Otherwise, Choristers and Verbena are usually adept at mass ritual involving sleepers which can generate some awesome results.<br /> Dreamspeakers generally have the ability to bargain with spirits using chiminage where most people attempt to bind spirits directly or call on Umbral protocol.<br /> I wonder if a more cryptology minded Euthanatos or a VA who feels his online person is the true him would be able to use True Names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T02:52:32-08:00","id":1161113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1158813-tradition-specific-abilities?p=1160881#post1160881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you including implicit benefits of certain groups like the less-paradox-prone aspects of technomagic? Otherwise, Choristers and Verbena are usually adept at mass ritual involving sleepers which can generate some awesome results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that it's the Verbenae True Mages and the Chorister True Mages who be able to do better Rituals involving many mundane humans, and not the Cult of Ecstasy True Mages? I think that the Cult of Ecstasy True Mages would be able to do such Rituals better than the Verbenae True Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T05:10:36-08:00","id":1161128,"title":"","content":"Probably because of religious ceremonialism that is commonly associated with the origins of those organizations. <br /> <br /> (Also, you don't have to repeatedly specify you're referring to the True Mages in those organizations. It it's implicit from the context of ritual magic and the flow of the conversation as a whole.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}